# LOAD-BEARING, unlike the inert per-connector .dockerignore files corrected in
# batch 1. Those sat beside a Dockerfile whose build context was the repo root, and
# Docker only reads .dockerignore at the CONTEXT root, so they were never consulted.
# Here the context IS this directory (`docker build -f ../../terraform/docker/
# dis-ui-ver2.Dockerfile ... .` from services/dis-ui-ver2), so Docker reads THIS file.
#
# Mirrors what dis/.gcloudignore already strips from the Cloud Build upload, so the
# local build and the Cloud Build finally see the same tree. Without it the
# Dockerfile's `COPY . .` overwrites the `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` layer with
# the host's node_modules, and the bundle is built against whatever is on the laptop
# rather than the lockfile - which is how the serving v15 was produced and why it was
# not reproducible by anyone else.
#
# .env* is the sharpest of these: `vite build` READS .env / .env.local from the
# context and would silently override the --build-arg values with a developer's local
# ones. It is gitignored (*.local), so it never shows up in review.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
.env
.env.*
*.local
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
